@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@attendanceUrl = {{baseUrl}}/attendance
@schoolId = 52426aab-497c-4880-8f8a-ad8a385f6e2b
@classId = e8b7f870-a406-40cf-a83d-a0e67bc16f7e
 @studentId = 238eb983-1d32-46b3-98e8-737741356055
@studentId2 = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@userId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000010
@date = 2026-02-15

### Note: With cookie-based authentication, ensure your HTTP client (like VS Code REST Client)
### automatically manages and sends cookies received from login responses (e.g., via a cookie jar).

# ================================================================
# SETUP
# ================================================================

### 0.1 Login as admin (prerequisite for every protected request)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "principal@school.test",
  "password": "PrincipalPass123",
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}"
}

### 0.2 Verify attendance settings (sanity check)
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/school/{{schoolId}}/settings


# ================================================================
# 1. MARKING
# ================================================================

### 1.1 Mark attendance for one student
# @name markOne
POST {{attendanceUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "studentId": "{{studentId}}",
  "classId": "{{classId}}",
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "status": "Present",
  "remarks": null
}

### 1.2 Re-mark same student (upsert) — should UPDATE, not error
POST {{attendanceUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "studentId": "{{studentId}}",
  "classId": "{{classId}}",
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "status": "Late",
  "remarks": "Arrived 8:15am"
}

### 1.3 Bulk mark the whole class
# @name bulkMark
POST {{attendanceUrl}}/bulk
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "classId": "{{classId}}",
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "entries": [
    { "studentId": "{{studentId}}", "status": "Present", "remarks": null },
    { "studentId": "{{studentId2}}", "status": "Absent", "remarks": "Sick" }
  ]
}

### 1.4 Bulk upsert (idempotent)
POST {{attendanceUrl}}/upsert
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "classId": "{{classId}}",
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "entries": [
    { "studentId": "{{studentId}}", "status": "Present", "remarks": "Corrected" }
  ]
}

### 1.5 Update a single record
### Prereq: @attendanceId from 1.1 response.attendance.id
@attendanceId = 0042d47d-d3e2-4a09-b70c-19844f67e52f

PUT {{attendanceUrl}}/{{attendanceId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Excused",
  "remarks": "Medical appointment"
}

### 1.6 Auto-mark missing students as absent
POST {{attendanceUrl}}/class/{{classId}}/date/{{date}}/auto-absent

### 1.7 Copy attendance from one day to another
POST {{attendanceUrl}}/copy
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "classId": "{{classId}}",
  "fromDate": "{{date}}",
  "toDate": "2026-11-03"
}

### 1.8 Import attendance from CSV rows
POST {{attendanceUrl}}/import
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "classId": "{{classId}}",
  "rows": [
    {
      "admissionNumber": "ADM-2027-001",
      "date": "2026-11-04",
      "status": "Present"
    },
    {
      "admissionNumber": "ADM-2026-002",
      "date": "2026-11-04",
      "status": "Absent",
      "remarks": "Family emergency"
    }
  ]
}

### 1.9 Delete an attendance record
DELETE {{attendanceUrl}}/{{attendanceId}}


# ================================================================
# 2. READS
# ================================================================

### 2.1 Get attendance by ID
### Prereq: @attendanceId from 1.1 response
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/{{attendanceId}}

### 2.2 Get one student's attendance on a date
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/student/{{studentId}}/date/{{date}}

### 2.3 Get student attendance history
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/student/{{studentId}}/history

### 2.4 Get student attendance history — filtered
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/student/{{studentId}}/history?fromDate=2026-11-01&toDate=2026-11-30&status=Absent

### 2.5 Get student attendance stats
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/student/{{studentId}}/stats

### 2.6 Get class attendance for a date
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/class/{{classId}}/date/{{date}}

### 2.7 Get class attendance summary
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/class/{{classId}}/date/{{date}}/summary

### 2.8 Get school attendance for a date
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/school/{{schoolId}}/date/{{date}}

### 2.9 Get monthly register for a class
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/class/{{classId}}/register?year=2026&month=11

### 2.10 List absentees for a date
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/school/{{schoolId}}/absentees?date={{date}}

### 2.11 List late arrivals for a date
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/school/{{schoolId}}/late-arrivals?date={{date}}

### 2.12 List chronic absentees (below 80%)
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/school/{{schoolId}}/chronic-absentees?threshold=80

### 2.13 List students not yet marked on a date
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/class/{{classId}}/date/{{date}}/not-marked

### 2.14 Get attendance audit trail
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/class/{{classId}}/date/{{date}}/audit


# ================================================================
# 3. ANALYTICS
# ================================================================

### 3.1 Attendance rate for a class
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/class/{{classId}}/rate

### 3.2 Attendance rate — filtered date range
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/class/{{classId}}/rate?fromDate=2026-11-01&toDate=2026-11-30

### 3.3 Count attendance by status
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/school/{{schoolId}}/by-status?date={{date}}

### 3.4 Attendance trend for a class (last 30 days)
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/class/{{classId}}/trend?days=30

### 3.5 Attendance by gender
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/school/{{schoolId}}/by-gender

### 3.6 School-wide attendance stats
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/school/{{schoolId}}/stats

### 3.7 Compare this month vs last month
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/school/{{schoolId}}/comparison


# ================================================================
# 4. HELPERS
# ================================================================

### 4.1 Validate a date (should succeed — valid date within term)
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/school/{{schoolId}}/validate-date?date=2026-11-02

### 4.2 Validate a future date (should fail with clear message)
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/school/{{schoolId}}/validate-date?date=2099-12-31

### 4.3 Check if a user can mark this class
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/user/{{userId}}/class/{{classId}}/can-mark

### 4.4 Get attendance settings
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/school/{{schoolId}}/settings


# ================================================================
# 5. NEGATIVE / VALIDATION TESTS
# ================================================================

### 5.1 Mark with invalid status — expect 400
POST {{attendanceUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "studentId": "{{studentId}}",
  "classId": "{{classId}}",
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "status": "Present-ish"
}

### 5.2 Mark with invalid UUID — expect 400
POST {{attendanceUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "not-a-uuid",
  "studentId": "{{studentId}}",
  "classId": "{{classId}}",
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "status": "Present"
}

### 5.3 Mark with malformed date — expect 400
POST {{attendanceUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "studentId": "{{studentId}}",
  "classId": "{{classId}}",
  "date": "2026-13-45",
  "status": "Present"
}

### 5.4 Mark a student not in the class — expect 400
POST {{attendanceUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "studentId": "{{studentId2}}",
  "classId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000099",
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "status": "Present"
}

### 5.5 Mark for a future date — expect 400
POST {{attendanceUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "studentId": "{{studentId}}",
  "classId": "{{classId}}",
  "date": "2099-12-31",
  "status": "Present"
}

### 5.6 Bulk mark with duplicate students — expect 400
POST {{attendanceUrl}}/bulk
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "classId": "{{classId}}",
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "entries": [
    { "studentId": "{{studentId}}", "status": "Present" },
    { "studentId": "{{studentId}}", "status": "Absent" }
  ]
}

### 5.7 Bulk mark with empty entries — expect 400
POST {{attendanceUrl}}/bulk
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "classId": "{{classId}}",
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "entries": []
}

### 5.8 Copy to the same date — expect 400
POST {{attendanceUrl}}/copy
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "classId": "{{classId}}",
  "fromDate": "{{date}}",
  "toDate": "{{date}}"
}

### 5.9 No auth — expect 401 (comment out login cookie or clear the jar first)
POST {{attendanceUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": "{{schoolId}}",
  "studentId": "{{studentId}}",
  "classId": "{{classId}}",
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "status": "Present"
}

### 5.10 Invalid attendance ID on read — expect 400
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/not-a-uuid

### 5.11 Chronic absentees with invalid threshold — expect 400
GET {{attendanceUrl}}/school/{{schoolId}}/chronic-absentees?threshold=200